flowchart TD
    A[Adding or updating a work on ORCID] --> B{Does the work<br/>already have a DOI?}

    B -->|Yes| D1[Use the DOI route:<br/>Zenodo / DataCite pushes<br/>to ORCID directly]
    D1 --> D2[Remove it from the<br/>BibTeX corpus —<br/>never import twice]
    D2 --> V

    B -->|No| C{Is the repository public?}
    C -->|"Yes, and a DOI is wanted"| C1[Offer the Zenodo route:<br/>enable repo, cut a release,<br/>Zenodo mints the DOI]
    C1 --> D2
    C -->|"No, or DOI not wanted"| E[BibTeX route]

    E --> E1{Is every claimed channel<br/>publicly reachable?}
    E1 -->|Probe it| E2[curl the URL and<br/>each store listing]
    E2 --> E3{200 / 301?}
    E3 -->|No| E4[OMIT that channel<br/>from note and url.<br/>Never claim it]
    E3 -->|Yes| E5[Include it]
    E4 --> F
    E5 --> F[Choose the work type]

    F --> F1{What kind of product?}
    F1 -->|"App, package, CLI, extension"| T1[Software]
    F1 -->|"Portfolio / brand site"| T2[Website]
    F1 -->|"Published documentation"| T3[Other or Website]

    T1 --> G
    T2 --> G
    T3 --> G[Write the entry<br/>see aoneahsan-cccs-bibtex]

    G --> H["Import into ORCID<br/>(owner only — needs login)"]
    H --> I[["🔴 Work arrives as type OTHER.<br/>No BibTeX type yields Software."]]
    I --> J[Record the retype as an<br/>owner-only MANUAL-TASKS row]
    J --> K[Owner retypes each work<br/>in the ORCID UI]
    K --> V

    V[Verify] --> V1[Every url resolves]
    V1 --> V2[Year = real first-release year,<br/>from git or npm — not today]
    V2 --> V3[No invented DOI,<br/>no unlisted channel claimed]
    V3 --> DONE([Done])

    style I fill:#ffe0e0,stroke:#c00
    style E4 fill:#fff4d6,stroke:#c90
    style DONE fill:#e0f0e0,stroke:#0a0
